<task>
Answer the job application questions for the posting at: {{.JobPostingUrl}}
</task>

<current_date>{{.CurrentDate}}</current_date>

<job_context>
  <job_posting_url>{{.JobPostingUrl}}</job_posting_url>
  <job_title>{{.JobTitle}}</job_title>
  <company_name>{{.CompanyName}}</company_name>
  <job_description>
{{.JobDescription}}
  </job_description>
</job_context>

<candidate>
  <candidate_profile>
{{.UserProfileJSON}}
  </candidate_profile>

  <candidate_resume>
{{.UserResume}}
  </candidate_resume>
</candidate>

<existing_application_answers>
{{.ExistingApplicationAnswers}}
</existing_application_answers>
{{if .PagesContext}}
<pages_context>
  {{range .PagesContext}}
  <page>
    <url>{{.Url}}</url>
    <content>
{{.Content}}
    </content>
  </page>
  {{end}}
</pages_context>
{{end}}
<questions_to_answer>
{{.QuestionsJSON}}
</questions_to_answer>

<instructions>
Answer every question in <questions_to_answer>. Echo each id unchanged. Use the candidate profile, resume, existing answers, job context, and <pages_context> when present. For motivation/fit questions, write a grounded answer that can subtly weave overlap between the company pages, job description, and resume. Prefer a short plain explanation over jargon; give a detailed answer only when the question asks for detail. If a factual question cannot be answered truthfully from the provided data, return an empty answer string for that question. Respond with the required JSON format.
</instructions>
